1
00:00:07,785 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,985 --> 00:01:39,025
ADAPTED FROM THE EARLY SPRING ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:02:19,385 --> 00:02:22,505
LOVE BEGINS ON A BITTERSWEET NOTE

4
00:02:29,545 --> 00:02:32,225
Why the long face? It's longer
than the filefish we serve here.

5
00:02:32,305 --> 00:02:34,945
Anyone who saw you
would think I'd served you fake liquor.

6
00:02:35,025 --> 00:02:36,585
-Save it.
-Drink with me.

7
00:02:43,825 --> 00:02:45,025
Trouble in love?

8
00:02:49,145 --> 00:02:50,425
As if.

9
00:02:54,025 --> 00:02:56,585
I guessed it, didn't I? So you're dating?

10
00:02:57,265 --> 00:02:58,825
We are,

11
00:02:58,905 --> 00:03:00,745
but we're keeping it secret.

12
00:03:01,425 --> 00:03:02,385
A secret relationship?

13
00:03:02,465 --> 00:03:03,865
It feels strange.

14
00:03:06,465 --> 00:03:08,985
Ms. Shang is a great girl.

15
00:03:09,065 --> 00:03:12,025
She's kind, hardworking, and dependable.

16
00:03:12,105 --> 00:03:13,865
And she looks at you

17
00:03:13,945 --> 00:03:16,145
like an adoring little fawn.

18
00:03:16,225 --> 00:03:17,545
What's not to like?

19
00:03:17,625 --> 00:03:19,865
You should at least make it official.

20
00:03:21,025 --> 00:03:22,465
You think I wanted to keep it secret?

21
00:03:23,945 --> 00:03:26,305
Whenever she sees me in public,
she avoids me like the plague,

22
00:03:26,945 --> 00:03:28,545
terrified someone might notice.

23
00:03:29,825 --> 00:03:32,745
And the two of us
can only see each other on weekends.

24
00:03:32,825 --> 00:03:34,185
Is that a normal relationship?

25
00:03:34,865 --> 00:03:36,705
It is a little unusual,

26
00:03:37,865 --> 00:03:39,385
but I can understand why.

27
00:03:40,505 --> 00:03:42,545
Ms. Shang has a strong sense of pride.

28
00:03:43,145 --> 00:03:44,425
She's afraid you'll look down on her

29
00:03:45,025 --> 00:03:48,025
and that your relationship
won't survive once it comes to light.

30
00:03:48,105 --> 00:03:49,745
In a way, she's protecting you.

31
00:03:50,385 --> 00:03:54,185
Besides, shouldn't you
be pleased that she knows

32
00:03:54,265 --> 00:03:57,305
how to conduct herself at work?
Why are you so bothered?

33
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:02,185
She made a mistake at work.

34
00:04:03,345 --> 00:04:04,465
I criticized her,

35
00:04:05,065 --> 00:04:06,505
and she still won't talk to me.

36
00:04:14,505 --> 00:04:15,505
There it is.

37
00:04:16,225 --> 00:04:17,585
You took the scenic route

38
00:04:18,465 --> 00:04:19,665
to get to the point.

39
00:04:20,265 --> 00:04:21,545
Did you make it up to her afterward?

40
00:04:23,225 --> 00:04:25,425
Other big-shot bosses
protect their girlfriends.

41
00:04:25,505 --> 00:04:26,785
But you?

42
00:04:26,865 --> 00:04:29,425
All stick and no carrot.

43
00:04:29,505 --> 00:04:32,305
What's she getting
out of this relationship?

44
00:04:35,145 --> 00:04:36,305
You don't get it.

45
00:04:36,905 --> 00:04:38,825
If she wants to grow quickly at work,

46
00:04:38,905 --> 00:04:40,465
she has to solve problems herself.

47
00:04:42,305 --> 00:04:43,825
She understands
that this is how she'll learn.

48
00:04:44,865 --> 00:04:46,065
And this time,

49
00:04:46,865 --> 00:04:47,985
she handled it pretty well.

50
00:04:48,905 --> 00:04:50,065
But she was too naive.

51
00:04:50,945 --> 00:04:54,745
She thought being loyal at work
would earn her loyalty in return.

52
00:04:56,185 --> 00:04:57,425
Foolish.

53
00:04:57,505 --> 00:04:58,945
You just said yourself

54
00:04:59,545 --> 00:05:03,265
that she did some things well.

55
00:05:03,785 --> 00:05:07,145
Everyone makes mistakes.
Just soften a little.

56
00:05:07,945 --> 00:05:09,105
How about this?

57
00:05:09,185 --> 00:05:10,745
Forget the gifts.

58
00:05:10,825 --> 00:05:13,105
But starting tomorrow,
send her flowers to show you're sorry.

59
00:05:13,785 --> 00:05:14,825
I did nothing wrong.

60
00:05:15,345 --> 00:05:16,545
Why should I send flowers?

61
00:05:16,625 --> 00:05:18,865
It's not like anything serious
happened between you two.

62
00:05:18,945 --> 00:05:20,465
Why does it matter who's right or wrong?

63
00:05:21,025 --> 00:05:23,105
If you want this relationship to work,

64
00:05:23,185 --> 00:05:24,985
send her flowers and smooth things over.

65
00:05:34,025 --> 00:05:35,385
Will flowers really work?

66
00:05:36,665 --> 00:05:37,745
Of course.

67
00:05:38,425 --> 00:05:40,105
Women go weak at the knees for flowers.

68
00:05:40,825 --> 00:05:41,825
I'll arrange it.

69
00:05:41,905 --> 00:05:43,265
Starting tomorrow, she'll get flowers

70
00:05:43,345 --> 00:05:46,145
until she's no longer mad.

71
00:05:56,345 --> 00:05:59,185
-Hello. I'm here to see Mr. Luan.
-Just go straight ahead.

72
00:05:59,865 --> 00:06:00,945
Please sign here.

73
00:06:04,505 --> 00:06:05,905
I've got some gossip.

74
00:06:07,785 --> 00:06:11,105
Boss has quietly set up a love nest.

75
00:06:13,225 --> 00:06:14,545
Huh?

76
00:06:14,625 --> 00:06:15,665
With whom?

77
00:06:16,985 --> 00:06:17,825
Her. Look.

78
00:06:31,145 --> 00:06:32,065
Luan Nian!

79
00:06:37,065 --> 00:06:40,265
Boss rented my grandmother's
courtyard house in the hutong.

80
00:06:40,345 --> 00:06:41,385
When I went to hand over the keys,

81
00:06:41,985 --> 00:06:43,505
this gorgeous woman was staying there.

82
00:06:44,185 --> 00:06:46,625
Her name is Zang Yao.
She's Luke's childhood friend.

83
00:06:47,425 --> 00:06:50,505
The classic childhood sweetheart.

84
00:06:51,425 --> 00:06:52,345
Hold on.

85
00:06:53,785 --> 00:06:56,505
Look how elegant she is.

86
00:06:56,585 --> 00:06:58,905
You can tell at a glance
she and Luke move in the same circles.

87
00:06:58,985 --> 00:07:00,145
Look.

88
00:07:00,665 --> 00:07:01,905
Look at this huge cake.

89
00:07:02,545 --> 00:07:05,105
She ordered it from Paris

90
00:07:05,185 --> 00:07:07,185
for Luke's birthday three years ago.

91
00:07:07,265 --> 00:07:08,545
I picked it up.

92
00:07:08,625 --> 00:07:11,465
Back then, she was still studying abroad.

93
00:07:12,865 --> 00:07:14,705
This time, Boss specifically said

94
00:07:15,225 --> 00:07:19,385
the house had to be nice and quiet,
and he didn't even haggle over the rent.

95
00:07:19,465 --> 00:07:22,185
Do you think they're really dating?

96
00:07:22,785 --> 00:07:26,625
If they are,
that's quite something for him.

97
00:07:27,665 --> 00:07:32,025
Can you imagine
what a man like him will be like

98
00:07:32,625 --> 00:07:33,945
when he's in love?

99
00:07:34,505 --> 00:07:35,665
That's nice.

100
00:07:37,065 --> 00:07:38,385
I still have a report to finish.

101
00:07:39,025 --> 00:07:40,305
I'd better get back to it.

102
00:07:43,905 --> 00:07:45,425
Look at that cake.

103
00:07:48,105 --> 00:07:50,265
Lumi, these flowers are for Mr. Luan.

104
00:07:56,305 --> 00:07:57,705
Something's definitely up.

105
00:08:00,665 --> 00:08:02,545
Weren't we meeting
at Tan Mian's restaurant?

106
00:08:04,945 --> 00:08:07,145
I'm almost off work.
Why did you come here?

107
00:08:08,225 --> 00:08:09,585
To pick you up.

108
00:08:09,665 --> 00:08:11,865
And let you ride in my new car.

109
00:08:13,385 --> 00:08:15,185
You just got back.
Where did you get a car?

110
00:08:15,265 --> 00:08:16,865
You rented me the house,

111
00:08:16,945 --> 00:08:18,705
and Song and the others arranged the car.

112
00:08:21,825 --> 00:08:22,905
Come in.

113
00:08:28,665 --> 00:08:30,745
Mr. Luan, your flowers.

114
00:08:31,865 --> 00:08:34,465
Is this the surprise
you prepared for me tonight?

115
00:08:34,545 --> 00:08:35,784
They're beautiful.

116
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:40,024
Lumi.

117
00:08:49,505 --> 00:08:50,425
Should I close the door, Mr. Luan?

118
00:08:51,265 --> 00:08:52,505
Thanks.

119
00:08:59,785 --> 00:09:00,425
LUAN NIAN

120
00:09:00,505 --> 00:09:01,545
Have you left?

121
00:09:39,505 --> 00:09:40,585
Tao.

122
00:09:44,065 --> 00:09:46,785
Get in. I'm driving everyone home.

123
00:09:52,705 --> 00:09:54,585
FATED FOR YOU

124
00:09:57,705 --> 00:09:58,945
Sun Yu,

125
00:09:59,025 --> 00:10:00,825
your company's so stingy.

126
00:10:01,345 --> 00:10:02,625
Such a big matchmaking event,

127
00:10:02,705 --> 00:10:04,385
and this beat-up
little van delivers the flowers.

128
00:10:04,465 --> 00:10:06,345
No wonder they say
poverty makes marriage miserable.

129
00:10:06,425 --> 00:10:08,585
If your members
see flowers arriving in this wreck,

130
00:10:08,665 --> 00:10:09,905
their dates won't stand a chance.

131
00:10:10,985 --> 00:10:12,865
I did my best
to uphold the company's image.

132
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:14,585
Can't you see how nicely I decorated it?

133
00:10:14,665 --> 00:10:17,025
I'm just a beggar here,
and beggars can't be choosers.

134
00:10:17,105 --> 00:10:18,625
It's fine. I think it's perfectly fine.

135
00:10:20,225 --> 00:10:22,225
You know what?
I bought those flowers wholesale.

136
00:10:22,305 --> 00:10:24,785
I'll pick out some nice ones
and put them in our place.

137
00:10:26,185 --> 00:10:27,025
Sun Yu.

138
00:10:29,065 --> 00:10:30,625
Could you give me a bouquet?

139
00:10:31,465 --> 00:10:33,505
Of course. We've got plenty.

140
00:10:39,145 --> 00:10:42,145
Cheer up. It's just a bouquet.
I'll give you one.

141
00:10:42,225 --> 00:10:43,465
Tell me what kind you want.

142
00:10:43,545 --> 00:10:44,705
I'll send it to your office tomorrow.

143
00:10:44,785 --> 00:10:45,785
You'll see a huge bouquet

144
00:10:45,865 --> 00:10:48,105
right in the middle of your desk.

145
00:10:48,185 --> 00:10:49,385
-How's that?
-Great.

146
00:10:49,985 --> 00:10:50,945
What are you two doing?

147
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:52,785
Am I invisible?

148
00:10:52,865 --> 00:10:55,105
You're sending her flowers? I'll do it.

149
00:10:56,145 --> 00:10:57,185
A different bouquet every day for a week.

150
00:10:57,265 --> 00:10:58,905
I'll outdo everyone at your office.

151
00:10:58,985 --> 00:11:01,745
With me around,
you'll get flowers every day.

152
00:11:01,825 --> 00:11:02,945
Homegrown and hand-delivered.

153
00:11:03,625 --> 00:11:07,345
-What are you talking about?
-A wise man once told me

154
00:11:07,425 --> 00:11:10,025
that if no one sends a girl flowers,
it means she has a special quality.

155
00:11:10,105 --> 00:11:11,105
What's that?

156
00:11:12,265 --> 00:11:13,505
She's naturally fragrant.

157
00:11:15,225 --> 00:11:16,825
Take a good sniff. What do you smell?

158
00:11:17,425 --> 00:11:18,545
What?

159
00:11:19,225 --> 00:11:20,545
-Flowers?
-Wrong!

160
00:11:20,625 --> 00:11:21,625
Peaches!

161
00:11:23,865 --> 00:11:26,625
-Right, peaches, Tao's fragrance.
-Keep your eyes on the road.

162
00:11:28,185 --> 00:11:32,145
FATED FOR YOU

163
00:11:47,145 --> 00:11:48,465
Flora, these are for you.

164
00:11:50,465 --> 00:11:51,825
-Thank you.
-No problem.

165
00:11:51,905 --> 00:11:52,825
Flora,

166
00:11:52,905 --> 00:11:55,105
-are you seeing someone?
-No.

167
00:11:55,745 --> 00:11:58,785
White lisianthus
symbolizes everlasting love.

168
00:11:59,305 --> 00:12:01,305
Your boyfriend is quite a romantic.

169
00:12:01,385 --> 00:12:02,265
Congratulations.

170
00:12:02,345 --> 00:12:03,345
-I don't have one.
-Who sent them?

171
00:12:03,425 --> 00:12:05,625
-Morning, Mr. Luan.
-Morning, Mr. Luan.

172
00:12:18,105 --> 00:12:19,065
HOPE THIS BRIGHTENS YOUR DAY

173
00:12:22,385 --> 00:12:23,785
I got the flowers.

174
00:12:23,865 --> 00:12:24,905
Thanks, Lei.

175
00:12:25,465 --> 00:12:26,225
SUNFLOWER FAMILY

176
00:12:26,305 --> 00:12:27,385
I haven't sent anything yet.

177
00:12:27,465 --> 00:12:28,825
You haven't given me your address.

178
00:12:29,505 --> 00:12:30,985
I didn't send them either.

179
00:12:31,585 --> 00:12:32,945
Was it Yuanzhu?

180
00:12:33,025 --> 00:12:34,225
Not me either.

181
00:12:34,305 --> 00:12:38,345
Looks like Tao has plenty of admirers.

182
00:12:38,425 --> 00:12:40,385
We should look into it.

183
00:12:40,465 --> 00:12:42,305
Love is in the air.

184
00:13:03,665 --> 00:13:05,105
Here. Your flowers.

185
00:13:05,185 --> 00:13:07,105
Five days in a row.

186
00:13:07,185 --> 00:13:08,665
Will this ever end?

187
00:13:08,745 --> 00:13:10,065
I just went through a breakup.

188
00:13:12,425 --> 00:13:13,305
What happened?

189
00:13:14,025 --> 00:13:16,665
He's always flirting around.
I caught him red-handed.

190
00:13:16,745 --> 00:13:19,465
He sent the exact same gift to two women.

191
00:13:19,545 --> 00:13:21,265
Of course,

192
00:13:21,345 --> 00:13:22,865
I dumped him.

193
00:13:23,545 --> 00:13:26,145
And now I have to watch you
get flowers every day. I can't take it.

194
00:13:27,505 --> 00:13:28,665
Lumi.

195
00:13:29,945 --> 00:13:32,465
Does the copy you submitted today
even make sense?

196
00:13:32,545 --> 00:13:33,625
Go fix it.

197
00:13:35,985 --> 00:13:37,185
The client needs it tomorrow.

198
00:13:41,225 --> 00:13:43,145
It's still early. Sneaking out already?

199
00:13:46,145 --> 00:13:47,065
No.

200
00:13:47,145 --> 00:13:50,185
I cleared it with Alex and Lumi.

201
00:13:50,265 --> 00:13:51,465
I'm leaving early.

202
00:13:53,465 --> 00:13:54,465
Where are you going?

203
00:13:56,265 --> 00:13:57,545
Hiking with some friends.

204
00:14:00,665 --> 00:14:01,985
Today's Friday.

205
00:14:05,625 --> 00:14:06,505
I know.

206
00:14:07,345 --> 00:14:09,065
We won't be back until Sunday.

207
00:14:13,505 --> 00:14:14,345
Have fun.

208
00:14:15,745 --> 00:14:16,945
Nice flowers.

209
00:14:18,705 --> 00:14:19,665
But they don't suit you.

210
00:14:21,945 --> 00:14:24,025
Then what flowers do you think suit me?

211
00:14:24,105 --> 00:14:25,505
Green foxtail.

212
00:14:47,785 --> 00:14:48,865
Let's go.

213
00:14:50,905 --> 00:14:53,225
What's wrong? You got flowers,
but you still seem down.

214
00:14:53,945 --> 00:14:55,585
-You can have them.
-Me?

215
00:15:38,305 --> 00:15:39,825
Watch your step, everyone.

216
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:43,985
Keep up.

217
00:15:45,585 --> 00:15:47,065
-Let's hit the restroom.
-All right.

218
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:49,505
Want water? I'll get several bottles.

219
00:15:49,585 --> 00:15:51,065
-Yes.
-OK.

220
00:15:51,145 --> 00:15:52,425
Hurry. I can't hold it much longer.

221
00:15:54,585 --> 00:15:56,585
Could the flowers be from Luan Nian?

222
00:15:56,665 --> 00:15:57,905
No way.

223
00:15:57,985 --> 00:15:59,865
He doesn't think I deserve flowers.

224
00:15:59,945 --> 00:16:01,665
Don't put yourself down like that.

225
00:16:02,345 --> 00:16:03,825
How many times have I told you?

226
00:16:06,785 --> 00:16:11,825
I wanted flowers because he gave
someone else flowers, and I got jealous.

227
00:16:17,345 --> 00:16:20,905
But I feel so silly,
comparing myself to her

228
00:16:20,985 --> 00:16:22,385
over a bouquet.

229
00:16:24,665 --> 00:16:25,945
You're not silly.

230
00:16:26,785 --> 00:16:28,705
Love makes you possessive.

231
00:16:28,785 --> 00:16:31,505
If you stopped feeling that way,
it'd mean you didn't love him anymore.

232
00:16:32,545 --> 00:16:33,625
Water. Here.

233
00:16:36,345 --> 00:16:37,625
Water. Here.

234
00:16:38,185 --> 00:16:39,065
Where did you buy it?

235
00:16:39,145 --> 00:16:40,305
-Let's go.
-Thanks.

236
00:16:40,385 --> 00:16:41,385
Aren't you two using the restroom?

237
00:16:41,465 --> 00:16:42,345
-Lei.
-No.

238
00:16:42,425 --> 00:16:43,825
-Let's start climbing.
-Come on.

239
00:16:43,905 --> 00:16:45,065
There won't be any restrooms up there.

240
00:16:46,865 --> 00:16:47,985
It's cold out here.

241
00:16:50,385 --> 00:16:52,105
Let me grab your backpack.
I'm getting tired.

242
00:16:53,105 --> 00:16:54,465
-You OK?
-Yes.

243
00:17:05,385 --> 00:17:06,985
It looks easier up there.

244
00:17:07,704 --> 00:17:08,625
Come on.

245
00:17:15,224 --> 00:17:17,265
Then what flowers do you think suit me?

246
00:17:18,464 --> 00:17:19,545
Green foxtail.

247
00:17:38,625 --> 00:17:39,985
What are your plans for New Year's Eve?

248
00:17:42,905 --> 00:17:45,665
Once the designers finalize the proposal,

249
00:17:45,745 --> 00:17:47,785
I'll be at the office overseeing

250
00:17:47,865 --> 00:17:49,785
the New Year's Eve
and New Year's Day ad launches.

251
00:17:53,145 --> 00:17:55,345
Do you have a passport and a snowboard?

252
00:17:56,865 --> 00:17:58,025
No.

253
00:18:01,385 --> 00:18:02,785
What's wrong? Getting tired?

254
00:18:04,345 --> 00:18:05,785
I just wanted a break.

255
00:18:05,865 --> 00:18:07,425
How do you have so much stamina?

256
00:18:07,505 --> 00:18:09,425
I grew up in the mountains.

257
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:11,585
Climbing was the best entertainment
we had as kids.

258
00:18:12,265 --> 00:18:13,225
No wonder.

259
00:18:16,705 --> 00:18:18,425
MOM

260
00:18:19,185 --> 00:18:22,305
When I was little,
I only got to go hiking on school trips,

261
00:18:22,385 --> 00:18:24,825
but before every trip, my dad would worry

262
00:18:24,905 --> 00:18:27,305
that I'd fall
and keep telling me to be careful.

263
00:18:28,305 --> 00:18:30,265
I can tell you grew up in a happy family.

264
00:18:30,945 --> 00:18:32,505
You can tell?

265
00:18:32,585 --> 00:18:35,105
You're innocent and cheerful.

266
00:18:35,185 --> 00:18:37,225
It's obvious your parents doted on you.

267
00:18:38,665 --> 00:18:39,625
They did.

268
00:18:39,705 --> 00:18:43,145
I don't think I've ever had
much to complain about.

269
00:18:46,065 --> 00:18:48,065
The man who drove you home last time…

270
00:18:48,145 --> 00:18:49,425
Is he your boyfriend?

271
00:18:54,145 --> 00:18:55,025
Sort of.

272
00:18:57,905 --> 00:18:59,665
Why aren't you dating anyone?

273
00:19:01,425 --> 00:19:02,825
I'd rather not make some poor girl suffer.

274
00:19:03,385 --> 00:19:06,385
What? Why would she suffer?

275
00:19:06,465 --> 00:19:09,865
I think anyone who dated you
would be very happy.

276
00:19:11,105 --> 00:19:12,425
Dating isn't important.

277
00:19:13,825 --> 00:19:15,025
Being together is what matters.

278
00:19:16,225 --> 00:19:17,425
What are you two talking about?

279
00:19:18,025 --> 00:19:20,025
Tao, come on. Keep up.

280
00:19:20,105 --> 00:19:22,065
-We're almost there.
-Coming!

281
00:19:23,025 --> 00:19:24,785
-Let's go.
-All right.

282
00:19:25,905 --> 00:19:27,105
Here.

283
00:19:27,185 --> 00:19:28,425
I'll pull you along.

284
00:19:28,505 --> 00:19:29,825
-It's all right.
-Come on.

285
00:19:40,025 --> 00:19:42,705
I've already talked to Song,
Tan Mian, and the others.

286
00:19:42,785 --> 00:19:44,785
How about we go snowboarding
in Northern Europe

287
00:19:45,305 --> 00:19:46,985
for our annual trip this year?

288
00:19:47,065 --> 00:19:48,185
BEIJING TO ZURICH

289
00:19:50,385 --> 00:19:52,185
FLIGHT BOOKING PAGE

290
00:20:09,065 --> 00:20:12,545
The view was worth the wait.

291
00:20:13,625 --> 00:20:14,785
It's breathtaking.

292
00:20:29,705 --> 00:20:31,505
I could jump
into this sea of clouds right now.

293
00:20:36,905 --> 00:20:38,505
You like clouds?

294
00:20:49,385 --> 00:20:50,385
Let's go up there and make a wish.

295
00:20:56,665 --> 00:20:59,985
I hope all my clients find their match.

296
00:21:00,065 --> 00:21:00,985
God of Wealth, God of Marriage,

297
00:21:01,065 --> 00:21:03,105
please work your magic! Please!

298
00:21:06,105 --> 00:21:07,385
Make me rich.

299
00:21:12,585 --> 00:21:13,985
What did you wish for?

300
00:21:14,745 --> 00:21:19,265
I just wished for my career

301
00:21:19,345 --> 00:21:20,505
to keep getting better!

302
00:21:20,585 --> 00:21:22,025
Great!

303
00:21:22,105 --> 00:21:24,105
Let my house go up in value!

304
00:21:24,185 --> 00:21:25,545
-Go up!
-Go up!

305
00:21:26,145 --> 00:21:27,585
Yuanzhu, what did you wish for?

306
00:21:29,425 --> 00:21:31,865
I'll be traveling
a lot for work after New Year's.

307
00:21:31,945 --> 00:21:34,705
I hope my autonomous
driving tests succeed.

308
00:21:35,985 --> 00:21:37,225
They definitely will.

309
00:21:37,905 --> 00:21:39,545
We worked so hard to get up here.

310
00:21:39,625 --> 00:21:40,465
How about a group photo?

311
00:21:40,545 --> 00:21:41,265
-Sure.
-Sounds good.

312
00:21:41,345 --> 00:21:42,065
-Come on.
-Come.

313
00:21:42,145 --> 00:21:43,305
-Move closer.
-Tao.

314
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:44,585
Move closer.

315
00:21:44,665 --> 00:21:45,745
One, two.

316
00:21:50,945 --> 00:21:51,825
Done.

317
00:21:51,905 --> 00:21:52,825
Let me be rich, please.

318
00:21:54,025 --> 00:21:55,465
It's getting pretty cold.

319
00:21:55,545 --> 00:21:57,385
Why don't we head down
and find something to eat?

320
00:21:57,465 --> 00:21:58,585
-Sure.
-I looked it up.

321
00:21:58,665 --> 00:22:00,585
The best food around here
is wood-fired chicken.

322
00:22:00,665 --> 00:22:02,225
-I've heard of it.
-Let's go.

323
00:22:02,305 --> 00:22:03,385
-Come on.
-Let's go.

324
00:22:03,465 --> 00:22:04,305
Yuanzhu's paying.

325
00:22:04,385 --> 00:22:05,425
-I'm freezing.
-Is it this way?

326
00:22:13,505 --> 00:22:14,945
Today is New Year's Eve.

327
00:22:15,025 --> 00:22:18,705
Beijing's evening rush hour
is expected to begin as early as 3 p.m.

328
00:22:18,785 --> 00:22:21,465
Please plan ahead if you're heading out.

329
00:22:21,545 --> 00:22:22,905
Public transportation is recommended.

330
00:22:32,425 --> 00:22:34,905
-Lumi, I'm leaving. Bye.
-I'm leaving as well.

331
00:22:34,985 --> 00:22:36,665
-Happy New Year.
-Happy New Year.

332
00:22:36,745 --> 00:22:37,825
Bye, Lumi.

333
00:22:37,905 --> 00:22:38,905
Take it easy. Don't drink too much.

334
00:22:42,345 --> 00:22:43,465
Flora,

335
00:22:45,065 --> 00:22:46,265
what are your plans for tonight?

336
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:50,385
I want to sleep all night.
I've been exhausted lately.

337
00:22:51,225 --> 00:22:52,265
Boring.

338
00:22:52,345 --> 00:22:53,265
I'm heading out, then.

339
00:22:53,345 --> 00:22:55,425
Traffic will be gridlocked everywhere.
Get home early.

340
00:22:55,505 --> 00:22:56,825
I'll leave once the client replies.

341
00:22:58,705 --> 00:22:59,945
LUAN NIAN: EVERYONE CAN LEAVE EARLY TODAY

342
00:23:00,025 --> 00:23:01,465
No need to wait.

343
00:23:01,545 --> 00:23:02,945
Luke's already celebrating
New Year's in Switzerland.

344
00:23:03,625 --> 00:23:05,705
Let's go. No one's here
to keep tabs on us.

345
00:23:06,465 --> 00:23:07,625
Happy New Year.

346
00:23:07,705 --> 00:23:09,305
-Happy New Year.
-Go on. Get going.

347
00:23:15,665 --> 00:23:17,665
SWITZERLAND

348
00:23:17,745 --> 00:23:19,145
I'm exhausted.

349
00:23:20,145 --> 00:23:21,865
The snow's really good this year.

350
00:23:21,945 --> 00:23:23,465
-The snow's good.
-I love my new board.

351
00:23:23,545 --> 00:23:24,705
But I wasn't at my best today.

352
00:23:24,785 --> 00:23:25,785
It's amazing.

353
00:23:25,865 --> 00:23:27,785
You need to practice
your carving next year. Seriously.

354
00:23:27,865 --> 00:23:30,185
I'm scared to go too fast. You know?

355
00:23:30,265 --> 00:23:31,785
It requires too much speed.

356
00:23:31,865 --> 00:23:33,865
And when you're going downhill,
you need to crouch lower.

357
00:23:34,705 --> 00:23:36,945
Come over here. Stop talking.

358
00:23:37,025 --> 00:23:38,185
Let's take a group photo.

359
00:23:38,785 --> 00:23:41,905
When we're old and gray,
we can look back on it.

360
00:23:41,985 --> 00:23:43,745
-I'll never grow old.
-Old and gray?

361
00:23:43,825 --> 00:23:44,505
I'll never…

362
00:23:44,585 --> 00:23:46,265
-Luan Nian, what are you doing?
-Luan Nian.

363
00:23:46,345 --> 00:23:47,385
-Luke, photo!
-Look at the camera.

364
00:23:47,465 --> 00:23:48,385
Hurry.

365
00:23:48,465 --> 00:23:49,505
-Come on.
-Let's take it.

366
00:23:49,585 --> 00:23:51,185
One, two, three.

367
00:23:52,065 --> 00:23:53,305
-Let me see.
-Let me see.

368
00:23:54,025 --> 00:23:56,105
-I'm so handsome.
-We didn't get him in it.

369
00:23:56,185 --> 00:23:58,265
-You blocked him.
-Let's go.

370
00:24:00,025 --> 00:24:02,985
What are you looking at?
You weren't even in the photo.

371
00:24:03,065 --> 00:24:03,985
Come on.

372
00:24:05,865 --> 00:24:08,185
One, two, three.

373
00:24:10,625 --> 00:24:11,465
-Come on.
-Let's drink.

374
00:24:11,545 --> 00:24:12,545
Cheers.

375
00:24:13,145 --> 00:24:14,465
Drink up, everyone.

376
00:24:16,265 --> 00:24:17,145
What's on your mind?

377
00:24:17,225 --> 00:24:18,505
You keep sitting here alone.

378
00:24:20,025 --> 00:24:21,145
I haven't snowboarded much
these past two years,

379
00:24:21,225 --> 00:24:23,065
so I was really off today.

380
00:24:23,145 --> 00:24:23,985
Want anything? I'll get it for you.

381
00:24:24,065 --> 00:24:25,945
No, thanks. You guys eat.

382
00:24:26,025 --> 00:24:27,745
-Honestly…
-Don't drink alone. Come join us.

383
00:24:29,665 --> 00:24:30,985
You always have to butt in.

384
00:24:36,865 --> 00:24:37,905
Luke,

385
00:24:38,465 --> 00:24:40,825
why don't you two
finally make it official on this trip?

386
00:24:48,105 --> 00:24:50,105
Have any of your relationships
ever worked out?

387
00:24:51,225 --> 00:24:52,985
Sure.

388
00:24:53,865 --> 00:24:56,425
Just… a few too many times.

389
00:24:57,505 --> 00:24:58,465
With disastrous results.

390
00:24:59,625 --> 00:25:00,945
That's why I'm worried about you.

391
00:25:02,145 --> 00:25:03,185
Yao.

392
00:25:04,465 --> 00:25:07,945
I've always felt like you've been
hiding something these past few years.

393
00:25:08,545 --> 00:25:09,825
How about I drink with you tonight,

394
00:25:09,905 --> 00:25:10,945
and you tell me
what's really on your mind?

395
00:25:11,545 --> 00:25:12,785
Cheers.

396
00:25:12,865 --> 00:25:15,425
Any secrets between us stay between us.

397
00:25:15,505 --> 00:25:17,225
Why would I tell you?

398
00:25:19,465 --> 00:25:20,705
All I know is

399
00:25:20,785 --> 00:25:23,505
that we've always
been really close friends.

400
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:26,305
But at the beginning,

401
00:25:26,385 --> 00:25:28,585
I don't think either of us
wanted to be just friends.

402
00:25:31,785 --> 00:25:32,625
Come on.

403
00:25:32,705 --> 00:25:33,625
Let's drink.

404
00:25:33,705 --> 00:25:34,745
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

405
00:25:36,785 --> 00:25:37,825
I have a girlfriend.

406
00:25:40,545 --> 00:25:41,385
What?

407
00:25:42,225 --> 00:25:43,785
Wait. You have a girlfriend?

408
00:25:43,865 --> 00:25:44,985
Since when?

409
00:25:45,785 --> 00:25:47,305
Are you serious?

410
00:25:47,385 --> 00:25:49,105
And you didn't even tell me?

411
00:25:49,185 --> 00:25:50,465
Do we know her?

412
00:25:50,545 --> 00:25:52,785
What's there to announce
about my love life?

413
00:25:53,945 --> 00:25:57,465
That's a pretty feeble excuse
for turning me down.

414
00:26:03,025 --> 00:26:04,225
Come on.

415
00:26:05,865 --> 00:26:06,905
Don't be upset.

416
00:26:06,985 --> 00:26:08,665
You know what Luan Nian's like.

417
00:26:09,265 --> 00:26:10,505
That's just how he talks.

418
00:26:13,945 --> 00:26:15,905
SIMPLY DELICIOUS

419
00:26:15,985 --> 00:26:17,745
What's wrong? What happened?

420
00:26:20,865 --> 00:26:22,225
I ran into my ex.

421
00:26:23,545 --> 00:26:25,825
He was spending
New Year's Eve with his girlfriend.

422
00:26:25,905 --> 00:26:27,265
And to make things worse,

423
00:26:28,465 --> 00:26:29,945
a coworker's event went wrong,

424
00:26:30,705 --> 00:26:32,505
and my boss tried
to make me take the blame.

425
00:26:34,185 --> 00:26:35,585
I refused,

426
00:26:35,665 --> 00:26:38,385
so he called me into his office
and chewed me out.

427
00:26:39,305 --> 00:26:41,145
There goes my year-end bonus.

428
00:26:42,025 --> 00:26:44,145
Don't cry, OK?

429
00:26:44,705 --> 00:26:47,705
Don't punish yourself
for other people's mistakes.

430
00:26:47,785 --> 00:26:49,665
Just ignore them.

431
00:26:49,745 --> 00:26:51,225
Don't you always take things in stride?

432
00:26:53,745 --> 00:26:54,945
But Tao,

433
00:26:56,745 --> 00:26:59,905
why is every step here so hard?

434
00:27:04,625 --> 00:27:06,825
We chose this path ourselves.

435
00:27:07,425 --> 00:27:08,705
You know what they say.

436
00:27:08,785 --> 00:27:13,865
Part of your salary
is for putting up with unfair treatment.

437
00:27:14,585 --> 00:27:16,185
And there's an old saying,

438
00:27:16,265 --> 00:27:20,065
if the road feels hard,
it's because we're going uphill.

439
00:27:20,945 --> 00:27:22,545
That means we're making progress,

440
00:27:22,625 --> 00:27:23,545
right?

441
00:27:27,865 --> 00:27:28,945
Right.

442
00:27:29,665 --> 00:27:30,865
Here.

443
00:27:30,945 --> 00:27:32,425
New Year's gifts for you.

444
00:27:34,585 --> 00:27:35,905
It's beautiful.

445
00:27:37,905 --> 00:27:39,185
Thank you.

446
00:27:39,265 --> 00:27:41,985
Oh my gosh. You even got us gifts.

447
00:27:42,705 --> 00:27:43,985
Thank you, Yuanzhu.

448
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:50,065
The world would be a better place
with more people like you.

449
00:27:52,465 --> 00:27:53,865
No more bad work.

450
00:27:54,625 --> 00:27:56,065
No more bad men.

451
00:27:57,865 --> 00:27:58,705
Well…

452
00:28:02,385 --> 00:28:04,865
There are always
a few truly awful men in the world,

453
00:28:04,945 --> 00:28:06,065
of truly awful men in the world,

454
00:28:06,145 --> 00:28:08,585
and you just happened to meet one of them.

455
00:28:12,825 --> 00:28:14,705
I… I'm not good at comforting people.

456
00:28:15,705 --> 00:28:18,825
How about I treat you to a movie later?

457
00:28:19,345 --> 00:28:20,425
OK.

458
00:28:21,225 --> 00:28:22,665
A midnight movie?

459
00:28:23,265 --> 00:28:24,505
I've never been to one.

460
00:28:24,585 --> 00:28:26,025
Neither have I.

461
00:28:26,105 --> 00:28:27,065
That's a shame.

462
00:28:27,145 --> 00:28:30,625
When I was in school, I was always broke.

463
00:28:30,705 --> 00:28:32,105
So during the holidays,

464
00:28:32,185 --> 00:28:35,025
my classmates and I
would always go to midnight movies.

465
00:28:35,105 --> 00:28:36,465
Great. Let's go after dinner.

466
00:28:37,065 --> 00:28:38,425
-OK.
-Great.

467
00:28:40,145 --> 00:28:41,985
It's New Year's Eve.

468
00:28:42,065 --> 00:28:43,385
I should cheer up.

469
00:28:45,345 --> 00:28:46,225
Pull it together.

470
00:28:48,065 --> 00:28:50,105
Let's take a group photo
and send it to Lei.

471
00:28:50,185 --> 00:28:52,705
It'll commemorate
our first New Year's Eve together.

472
00:28:52,785 --> 00:28:54,585
-OK.
-Hold on.

473
00:28:54,665 --> 00:28:56,265
I brought some props.

474
00:28:56,345 --> 00:28:57,345
You brought props?

475
00:28:57,425 --> 00:28:58,625
We need to get into the New Year's spirit.

476
00:28:59,665 --> 00:29:00,505
This one's for you.

477
00:29:01,425 --> 00:29:03,185
-OK.
-And this one's for you.

478
00:29:05,265 --> 00:29:06,745
-Do we put them on?
-I'll show you.

479
00:29:06,825 --> 00:29:08,225
Put it on,

480
00:29:08,825 --> 00:29:10,025
like this.

481
00:29:12,865 --> 00:29:14,145
So childish. So childish.

482
00:29:27,065 --> 00:29:29,465
Why did you say that?
When did you get a girlfriend?

483
00:29:30,905 --> 00:29:31,825
Go check on her.

484
00:29:39,705 --> 00:29:41,665
How was I supposed to know
he had a girlfriend?

485
00:29:46,265 --> 00:29:48,385
Zang Yao, let's talk outside.

486
00:30:07,825 --> 00:30:09,705
Do we have to talk about this
on New Year's Eve?

487
00:30:11,185 --> 00:30:12,545
You know,

488
00:30:12,625 --> 00:30:15,665
this could ruin
every New Year's Eve for me.

489
00:30:18,225 --> 00:30:20,785
I don't remember ever expressing
any special feelings for you.

490
00:30:22,785 --> 00:30:24,505
I only wanted us to be family

491
00:30:25,265 --> 00:30:26,345
and best friends.

492
00:30:42,865 --> 00:30:44,225
I got the wrong idea.

493
00:30:47,745 --> 00:30:49,305
I'm sorry if I hurt you.

494
00:30:52,825 --> 00:30:54,105
You don't have to apologize.

495
00:30:54,945 --> 00:30:57,905
You're Luan Nian, after all.
Luan Nian never admits he's wrong.

496
00:31:10,785 --> 00:31:12,225
Do you really have a girlfriend?

497
00:31:16,105 --> 00:31:17,145
Yes.

498
00:31:22,505 --> 00:31:23,465
All right.

499
00:31:24,185 --> 00:31:25,585
Then I'm happy for you.

500
00:31:29,305 --> 00:31:31,065
I hope I haven't ruined
your New Year's Eve.

501
00:31:31,745 --> 00:31:33,425
You haven't.

502
00:31:34,985 --> 00:31:38,065
I don't know why
she isn't here with you today,

503
00:31:39,745 --> 00:31:42,305
but since we're here,
we should enjoy ourselves.

504
00:31:44,665 --> 00:31:45,625
I'm going inside.

505
00:31:55,385 --> 00:31:57,105
Is it almost midnight?

506
00:31:57,185 --> 00:31:58,025
Time for the countdown.

507
00:31:58,785 --> 00:31:59,905
Time for the countdown.

508
00:32:04,545 --> 00:32:06,065
SHANG ZHITAO

509
00:32:09,625 --> 00:32:10,825
Ten.

510
00:32:10,905 --> 00:32:11,745
Nine.

511
00:32:11,825 --> 00:32:12,945
Eight.

512
00:32:13,025 --> 00:32:14,265
Seven.

513
00:32:14,345 --> 00:32:15,905
Six. Five.

514
00:32:16,505 --> 00:32:17,345
Four.

515
00:32:17,425 --> 00:32:18,385
Three.

516
00:32:18,465 --> 00:32:19,385
Two.

517
00:32:19,465 --> 00:32:20,705
One!

518
00:32:22,105 --> 00:32:23,305
Happy New Year!

519
00:32:25,465 --> 00:32:26,385
Are you out?

520
00:32:27,985 --> 00:32:30,625
I'm celebrating New Year's
with my friends.

521
00:32:31,465 --> 00:32:32,585
Happy New Year.

522
00:32:37,025 --> 00:32:40,665
I hope you and your friends
have a great time.

523
00:32:46,905 --> 00:32:49,745
If you're free tomorrow,
go to my place and check on my fish.

524
00:32:50,665 --> 00:32:51,865
You know the door code.

525
00:32:55,305 --> 00:32:56,505
Sure.

526
00:33:13,465 --> 00:33:15,105
-Happy New Year.
-Cheers.

527
00:33:15,185 --> 00:33:16,145
Happy New Year.

528
00:33:16,225 --> 00:33:18,865
I'm glad I have you guys. Thank you.

529
00:33:19,665 --> 00:33:20,785
Feeling better now?

530
00:33:25,585 --> 00:33:26,985
To the New Year!

531
00:33:29,785 --> 00:33:30,985
Do you think

532
00:33:32,505 --> 00:33:34,425
Switzerland is cold?

533
00:33:34,505 --> 00:33:35,345
Switzerland?

534
00:33:36,305 --> 00:33:37,385
It's not too bad.

535
00:33:37,465 --> 00:33:38,945
It has a temperate monsoon climate.

536
00:33:39,025 --> 00:33:44,865
Compared with Harbin,
Switzerland is just cool.

537
00:33:45,665 --> 00:33:46,505
Right.

538
00:33:47,985 --> 00:33:50,385
Then I must be a fake Harbin native.

539
00:33:50,465 --> 00:33:51,585
I'm really sensitive to the cold.

540
00:33:51,665 --> 00:33:54,825
Every winter, I wear layer after layer.

541
00:33:54,905 --> 00:33:55,825
That's good.

542
00:33:56,345 --> 00:33:57,585
You know how to keep warm.

543
00:33:59,225 --> 00:34:00,065
Come on.

544
00:34:00,145 --> 00:34:01,265
Happy New Year.

545
00:34:01,345 --> 00:34:02,545
Happy New Year.

546
00:34:21,784 --> 00:34:23,545
BAR

547
00:34:28,264 --> 00:34:30,705
Verified. Please open the door.

548
00:34:36,865 --> 00:34:39,985
Luke, how should I take care of your fish?

549
00:34:40,905 --> 00:34:42,185
Listen carefully and do exactly as I say.

550
00:34:48,425 --> 00:34:50,145
Replace the filter pad in the fish tank.

551
00:34:53,824 --> 00:34:55,744
The pads are in the cabinet
under the staghorn fern.

552
00:35:03,785 --> 00:35:05,145
There are gloves in the box.

553
00:35:05,225 --> 00:35:06,065
LUAN NIAN

554
00:35:09,145 --> 00:35:12,545
Open the cabinet under the tank
and find the filter first.

555
00:35:15,625 --> 00:35:17,625
Take out the old filter pad,

556
00:35:17,705 --> 00:35:18,785
then put the new one in.

557
00:35:24,345 --> 00:35:25,985
Check the thermometer beside it.

558
00:35:27,305 --> 00:35:29,625
Make sure the water temperature is right,
then add a little fish food.

559
00:35:31,185 --> 00:35:32,305
Luan Nian, come.

560
00:35:33,825 --> 00:35:34,785
Just follow my instructions.

561
00:35:35,545 --> 00:35:36,745
I'm hanging up.

562
00:36:12,225 --> 00:36:14,305
Verified. Please open the door.

563
00:36:38,145 --> 00:36:40,185
I hope you and the fish

564
00:36:40,265 --> 00:36:43,825
get everything you wish for
in the new year.

565
00:36:54,545 --> 00:36:55,585
TAN MIAN

566
00:36:56,985 --> 00:36:57,825
Hello?

567
00:36:57,905 --> 00:36:59,625
Seriously?

568
00:36:59,705 --> 00:37:02,225
We woke up
and were told you'd checked out.

569
00:37:02,305 --> 00:37:03,185
You're back in Beijing?

570
00:37:04,265 --> 00:37:05,385
Yeah.

571
00:37:05,465 --> 00:37:07,705
Did you go to see Ms. Shang?

572
00:37:07,785 --> 00:37:08,905
None of your business.

573
00:38:16,785 --> 00:38:21,185
POSTS ABOUT SWITZERLAND

574
00:38:31,105 --> 00:38:31,945
ZANG YAO: VISIT SWITZERLAND
WITH THE PEOPLE YOU LOVE AT LEAST ONCE

575
00:38:32,025 --> 00:38:33,145
GET A LITTLE TIPSY, LOOK AT ONE ANOTHER
AND SAY, "LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER."

576
00:38:52,105 --> 00:38:53,225
I…

577
00:38:55,305 --> 00:38:56,305
I'm in a relationship

578
00:38:57,785 --> 00:38:59,185
that isn't right.

579
00:39:00,345 --> 00:39:03,465
I always thought
I didn't care how it'd end

580
00:39:04,465 --> 00:39:10,745
or that I never expected a happy ending.

581
00:39:12,305 --> 00:39:13,945
But that isn't true.

582
00:39:16,825 --> 00:39:17,705
I'm…

583
00:39:18,425 --> 00:39:19,505
I'm awful.

584
00:39:19,585 --> 00:39:20,825
You're not awful.

585
00:39:26,585 --> 00:39:27,705
You're still young.

586
00:39:29,065 --> 00:39:30,785
Being young means you have
the chance to make mistakes.

587
00:39:32,065 --> 00:39:33,745
Never settle for less than you deserve.

588
00:39:35,105 --> 00:39:36,945
I believe you have the courage
to break out of your shell.

589
00:39:38,425 --> 00:39:39,785
Even if you don't yet,

590
00:39:40,545 --> 00:39:41,865
you will someday.

591
00:40:00,385 --> 00:40:01,865
Shang Zhitao, I'm coming to see you now.

592
00:40:13,345 --> 00:40:17,865
The classic childhood sweetheart.

593
00:40:17,945 --> 00:40:20,385
You can tell at a glance
she and Luke move in the same circles.

594
00:40:20,465 --> 00:40:23,505
Do you think they're really dating?

595
00:40:32,425 --> 00:40:33,945
Aren't you cold dressed like this?

596
00:40:38,425 --> 00:40:40,025
This is from the ski resort.

597
00:40:44,145 --> 00:40:45,185
I don't know how to snowboard.

598
00:40:47,065 --> 00:40:48,145
You can learn.

599
00:40:56,705 --> 00:40:58,025
I've realized…

600
00:41:01,305 --> 00:41:03,265
we're from completely different worlds.

601
00:41:09,505 --> 00:41:11,265
I don't know how to snowboard,

602
00:41:11,345 --> 00:41:13,145
and I don't want to learn for now

603
00:41:13,745 --> 00:41:15,745
because the ski passes are expensive.

604
00:41:16,665 --> 00:41:18,985
And I certainly wouldn't go
to Switzerland just to snowboard.

605
00:41:19,825 --> 00:41:23,385
Sorry to let
such an expensive gift go to waste.

606
00:41:28,265 --> 00:41:30,705
Are you still upset
about what happened at work?

607
00:41:32,225 --> 00:41:36,105
Didn't you say we should keep things
strictly professional at work?

608
00:41:36,705 --> 00:41:38,905
If you're unhappy with the way
I handled it, you can talk to me.

609
00:41:38,985 --> 00:41:41,105
Why bring it into our relationship?

610
00:41:42,785 --> 00:41:44,505
This isn't about work.

611
00:41:48,665 --> 00:41:50,025
You said before

612
00:41:51,305 --> 00:41:54,065
that if either of us
stopped liking the other,

613
00:41:54,145 --> 00:41:55,465
we could end things.

614
00:42:01,305 --> 00:42:02,585
Is there someone else?

615
00:42:03,345 --> 00:42:04,345
No.

616
00:42:04,425 --> 00:42:06,185
Then what do you mean? Just say it.

617
00:42:08,265 --> 00:42:09,505
I mean,

618
00:42:10,345 --> 00:42:13,025
if you start seeing someone else,
you have to tell me.

619
00:42:16,665 --> 00:42:18,425
You must be delusional.

620
00:42:18,505 --> 00:42:20,145
Do you think I sleep
with someone everywhere I go?

621
00:42:20,225 --> 00:42:22,265
Do you think every woman
I meet is after me?

622
00:43:01,625 --> 00:43:02,985
Are you all right?

623
00:43:03,065 --> 00:43:04,145
Let me see.

624
00:43:06,385 --> 00:43:08,545
Good grief. Your forehead's
hot enough to fry an egg.

625
00:43:08,625 --> 00:43:09,905
You have a fever.

626
00:43:11,585 --> 00:43:13,025
I do feel a little warm.

627
00:43:15,625 --> 00:43:16,745
Go home right now.
Why are you still working?

628
00:43:16,825 --> 00:43:18,665
-Go.
-I haven't filed for sick leave yet.

629
00:43:18,745 --> 00:43:20,025
Don't worry about it.

630
00:43:20,105 --> 00:43:22,745
I've got a stack of sick leave forms
in my drawer. Go home.

631
00:43:54,985 --> 00:43:57,145
LUAN NIAN

632
00:44:10,305 --> 00:44:12,225
Lumi says you have a fever.

633
00:44:12,745 --> 00:44:13,905
Is it bad?

634
00:44:13,985 --> 00:44:15,025
Have you been to the hospital?

635
00:44:15,625 --> 00:44:17,505
Do you want me to come over now?

636
00:44:17,585 --> 00:44:18,705
Answer me.

637
00:44:26,145 --> 00:44:28,145
LUAN NIAN

638
00:44:33,065 --> 00:44:34,105
Open the door.

639
00:45:08,425 --> 00:45:09,465
Don't take pictures.

640
00:45:10,145 --> 00:45:11,105
These aren't for you.

641
00:45:11,705 --> 00:45:13,465
I don't care who they're for.

642
00:45:13,545 --> 00:45:14,545
First come, first served.

643
00:45:15,985 --> 00:45:18,265
There isn't a love letter
in here, is there?

644
00:45:20,665 --> 00:45:22,505
Buy your own if you like them.

645
00:45:24,985 --> 00:45:27,225
You're no fun.

646
00:45:27,305 --> 00:45:28,785
It's just a bouquet.

647
00:45:29,385 --> 00:45:31,385
If I take it,
you can just buy another one.

648
00:45:32,345 --> 00:45:35,425
And here I was planning to invite you over
for a housewarming dinner tonight.

649
00:45:36,385 --> 00:45:37,905
I just learned on my phone

650
00:45:37,985 --> 00:45:40,105
how to make egg fried rice.

651
00:45:40,185 --> 00:45:42,025
I was going to show off my skills.

652
00:45:42,105 --> 00:45:44,825
Go to Tan Mian's restaurant
if you want something to eat.

653
00:45:44,905 --> 00:45:47,585
If you burn down the courtyard house,
I can't afford to pay for it.

654
00:45:49,905 --> 00:45:51,465
You'd even cover the damages for me?

655
00:45:52,785 --> 00:45:54,025
That alone proves

656
00:45:54,105 --> 00:45:57,145
all these years of friendship
weren't for nothing.

657
00:45:57,745 --> 00:45:58,745
By the way,

658
00:45:58,825 --> 00:46:01,425
I've talked to Song, Tan Mian,
and the others.

659
00:46:01,505 --> 00:46:05,265
How about we take
our annual trip over New Year's

660
00:46:05,345 --> 00:46:07,185
and go snowboarding in Northern Europe?

661
00:46:08,465 --> 00:46:10,825
I've already set the dates.
You can't miss it.

662
00:46:13,985 --> 00:46:16,865
You won't have that much work
over New Year's, will you?

663
00:46:19,665 --> 00:46:20,505
We'll see.

664
00:46:21,585 --> 00:46:23,745
No. You have to come.

665
00:46:26,225 --> 00:46:27,385
It's almost time.

666
00:46:28,745 --> 00:46:30,985
Get ready. We should go.

667
00:46:31,065 --> 00:46:32,385
I'm going to the restroom.

668
00:46:43,705 --> 00:46:46,505
TO SHANG ZHITAO: HAVE YOU LEFT?

